  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0004 database is a comprehensive system for managing a WordPress website, storing information about users, posts, comments, links, and site settings. The database contains 16 tables, each representing a distinct entity within the website. The wp_users table stores information about registered users, including their login credentials, email addresses, and display names. The wp_usermeta table links user metadata, such as custom fields, to the corresponding user IDs. The wp_posts table contains all the content published on the website, including posts, pages, and other types of content, with each post linked to its author and parent post. The wp_postmeta table stores additional metadata for each post, such as custom fields and tags. The wp_terms, wp_termmeta, and wp_term_taxonomy tables manage the website's taxonomy system, including categories and tags. The wp_term_relationships table links terms to the posts they are associated with. The wp_comments table stores all comments made on the website, linked to the posts they are commenting on and the users who made them. The wp_commentmeta table stores additional metadata for each comment. The wp_links table stores information about links, including their URLs, names, and descriptions. The wp_options table stores site-wide settings and options. The wp_registration_log table tracks user registration activity, including IP addresses and dates. The wp_site table stores information about the website itself, including its domain and path. The wp_sitemeta table stores site metadata, linked to the site ID. The wp_signups table stores information about signups, including user login credentials, email addresses, and activation keys.",
  "gold_question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThe project involves developing an open-source PHP-based Content Management System (CMS) that serves as a flexible platform for creating websites, blogs, or applications. This CMS is widely adopted by millions of users globally, ranging from individual creators and small businesses to large enterprises. It provides a customizable and intuitive user experience tailored for both beginners and advanced users.\n\n2) Objectives\n\n- Create a platform to build and customize websites seamlessly.\n- Enable real-time, code-free design and content editing.\n- Offer extensibility through a robust library of plugins and themes.\n- Facilitate integration with social media, analytics, and e-commerce features.\n- Support community interaction via comment tools and discussion forums.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Site Owners: Individuals and organizations who build and manage websites.\n- Developers: Those extending or customizing the CMS functionality.\n- End Users: Visitors engaging with websites built on the platform.\n- Plugin/Theme Developers: Creators expanding the CMS's features and design options.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Theme Management: Select from thousands of themes; upload custom themes easily.\n- Content Editing: Intuitive block-based editor for real-time content updates.\n- Plugin System: Access thousands of plugins to add functionalities like galleries, forums, SEO, and spam protection.\n- E-Commerce Support: Add online store capabilities with third-party integrations.\n- Comment System: Manage discussions with comment moderation tools.\n- Analytics & SEO: Integrate with analytics tools and optimize for search engines.\n- Social Media Integration: Link and share across various social media platforms.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability: Sustain a diverse range of website sizes and types.\n- Usability: Provide a user-friendly interface requiring no coding skills.\n- Performance: Ensure smooth operation under high traffic conditions.\n- Security: Incorporate measures to protect against vulnerabilities.\n- Extensibility: Facilitate easy integration of new features via an extensive directory of themes and plugins.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0004.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0004\nCREATE TABLE `wp_users` (\n  `ID` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_login` varchar(60) NOT NULL,\n  `user_pass` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `user_email` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `display_name` varchar(250) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `wp_usermeta` (\n  `umeta_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `meta_key` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `meta_value` longtext DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`umeta_id`),\n  KEY `user_id` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `wp_usermeta_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `wp_users` (`ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `wp_posts` (\n  `ID` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `post_author` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `post_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `post_content` longtext NOT NULL,\n  `post_title` text NOT NULL,\n  `post_status` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `post_type` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `post_parent` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`ID`),\n  KEY `post_author` (`post_author`),\n  CONSTRAINT `wp_posts_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_author`) REFERENCES `wp_users` (`ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `wp_postmeta` (\n  `meta_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `meta_key` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `meta_value` longtext DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`meta_id`),\n  KEY `post_id` (`post_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `wp_postmeta_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `wp_posts` (`ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `wp_terms` (\n  `term_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(200) NOT NULL,\n  `slug` varchar(200) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`term_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `wp_termmeta` (\n  `meta_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `term_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `meta_key` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `meta_value` longtext DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`meta_id`),\n  KEY `term_id` (`term_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `wp_termmeta_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`term_id`) REFERENCES `wp_terms` (`term_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `wp_term_taxonomy` (\n  `term_taxonomy_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `term_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `taxonomy` varchar(32) NOT NULL,\n  `description` longtext DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`term_taxonomy_id`),\n  KEY `term_id` (`term_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `wp_term_taxonomy_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`term_id`) REFERENCES `wp_terms` (`term_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `wp_term_relationships` (\n  `object_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `term_taxonomy_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`object_id`, `term_taxonomy_id`),\n  KEY `term_taxonomy_id` (`term_taxonomy_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `wp_term_relationships_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`object_id`) REFERENCES `wp_posts` (`ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `wp_term_relationships_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`term_taxonomy_id`) REFERENCES `wp_term_taxonomy` (`term_taxonomy_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `wp_comments` (\n  `comment_ID` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `post_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `comment_content` text NOT NULL,\n  `comment_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`comment_ID`),\n  KEY `post_id` (`post_id`),\n  KEY `user_id` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `wp_comments_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`post_id`) REFERENCES `wp_posts` (`ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `wp_comments_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `wp_users` (`ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `wp_commentmeta` (\n  `meta_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `comment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `meta_key` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `meta_value` longtext DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`meta_id`),\n  KEY `comment_id` (`comment_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `wp_commentmeta_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`comment_id`) REFERENCES `wp_comments` (`comment_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `wp_links` (\n  `link_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `link_url` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `link_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `link_description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`link_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `wp_options` (\n  `option_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `option_name` varchar(191) NOT NULL,\n  `option_value` longtext NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`option_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `option_name` (`option_name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `wp_registration_log` (\n  `log_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `ip_address` varchar(45) NOT NULL,\n  `registration_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`log_id`),\n  KEY `user_id` (`user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `wp_registration_log_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `wp_users` (`ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `wp_site` (\n  `site_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `domain` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `path` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`site_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `wp_sitemeta` (\n  `meta_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `site_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `meta_key` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `meta_value` longtext DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`meta_id`),\n  KEY `site_id` (`site_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `wp_sitemeta_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`site_id`) REFERENCES `wp_site` (`site_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `wp_signups` (\n  `signup_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `user_login` varchar(60) NOT NULL,\n  `user_email` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  `activation_key` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`signup_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
